{# Partnership levels as struck seals.

   Not a pricing table: there are no prices, and a five-column pricing grid
   with "To be announced" in every cell would advertise the gap rather than
   hold the position. A rank of seals says "five levels exist, in this order"
   without implying a price list is imminent.

   Rank is encoded three ways — disc size, number of struck rules, and the
   written name — so it survives greyscale and colour-blindness. See the
   .tiers block in style.css. #}
<ul class="tiers">
  {% for t in summit.sponsorshipTiers %}
  <li class="tier tier--{{ t.slug }}">
    <span class="tier__seal">
      {% set markName = t.mark %}{% include "components/mark.njk" %}
    </span>
    <span class="tier__rules" aria-hidden="true">
      {% for n in range(0, 6 - t.rank) %}<span></span>{% endfor %}
    </span>
    <span class="tier__name">{{ t.name }}</span>
    <span class="tier__status">Open</span>
  </li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
